*   **Schedule C (Profit or Loss From Business):** Used to report your $19,700 in 1099-NEC income and deduct your freelance expenses (supplies, home office).
*   **Schedule SE (Self-Employment Tax):** Used to calculate the Social Security and Medicare taxes on your freelance profit.
*   **Form 8829 (Expenses for Business Use of Your Home):** You only need this if you choose the "Regular Method" for your home office deduction. If you use the Simplified Method, it goes directly on Schedule C.

